The pre-amplifier gain, algorithm, power, and noise figure all contribute to the overall noise variance and system noise temperature. The choice of algorithm (e.g., AWGN, Rician, Rayleigh) and the receiver's noise bandwidth further influence the noise variance. The path loss formula, given by \( \text{gr}_{kl} = \left( \frac{1}{4\pi^2} \right) \left( \frac{d^2}{\lambda^2} \right) \), quantifies the impact of distance and wavelength on signal strength.

