\[ \text{SNR} = \frac{\text{P1}}{\sigma_{r kl}^2} \]
\[ \text{SINR} = \frac{\text{P4}}{\sigma_{r kl}^2 + \sigma_{n kl}^2} \]
where \(\sigma_{n kl}\) is the noise power density.

The noise variance is also affected by the satellite's geometry, with the SNR and SINR potentially varying based on the user's position relative to the satellite. In LEO systems, the SNR and SINR can be influenced by the user's distance from the satellite, as well as the satellite's angle of incidence on the user.

