The defocused feed array (DFA) placement in DBF architectures for satellite communications aims to optimize coverage by minimizing scan loss and maintaining signal quality even when feed elements fail. The defocused reflector, designed to focus feed elements at the borders of the array, is more robust to element failures. It reduces the loss of signal strength in the direction of failed elements compared to conventional reflectors, which focus feed elements at the center. This design choice ensures that even with some feed elements failing, the system remains operational with reduced degradation in signal strength. The defocused reflector maintains or improves signal quality, making it a more reliable solution.

